            "review_title": "Review at Bánh Xèo Phùng Hưng",
            "review_text": "Dương Minh Thông\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam48 contributions\n0\nLocal Banh Xeo in Phung Hung Market ✨\nAug 2025 • Family\nThis place is insanely crowded — right in the heart of the dining section at Phung Hung Market.\n\nFor me, the dishes here are decent for the price, but a bit bland compared to my taste, except for the bánh xèo (~4$ for a special one with egg, pork, shrimp, and squid cake) — that one was really delicious.\n\nSince the place is always packed, service can get a little messy and slow, but the owner and staff are so nice that you can’t really get mad at them. It’s inside the market, so I didn’t expect much in terms of ambiance — actually, I think eating like this once in a while is pretty fun.\n\nFor foreign visitors, I’d recommend going with a local friend or having a translation app ready, since orders are taken on paper and there’s no English menu.\nRead more\nWritten August 13, 2025",
